# {{name}}

A juiz component written in C++. It was made with `juiz pkg create --idl` of juiz {{juiz_version}},
from the process / container declarations of `{{idl_main}}`.

License: {{license}}

## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `{{idl_main}}` | The types and the declarations (JIDL) |
| `src/{{name}}.cpp` | The Component. Each `COMPONENT_*_FACTORY` is a type, listed in `{{name}}_component_manifest()`. Write the bodies (`throw`) |
| `CMakeLists.txt` | Builds the plugin with libjuiz_sdk (`find_package(juiz_sdk {{juiz_version}} EXACT)`), and generates the C++ types of the `.jidl` (`juiz_generate_types`, `juiz_idl.h`) |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz version) |
| `scripts/dev.sh`, `scripts/dev.ps1` | Build the plugin and put it with libjuiz_sdk in `app/plugins/<target>/` |
| `scripts/pack.sh`, `scripts/pack.ps1` | Build in release mode and make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |

## Requirements

- juiz {{juiz_version}} (`juiz --version`). Install it with `cargo install juiz_app --version {{juiz_version}}` or `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}`
- juiz in PATH when you build (CMake runs `juiz idl` to generate the C++ types of the `.jidl`)
- CMake 3.16 or later and a C++17 compiler (on Windows, Visual Studio 2022 with "Desktop development with C++")
- libjuiz_sdk {{juiz_version}} in `~/.juiz/sdk/{{juiz_version}}` (`%USERPROFILE%\.juiz\sdk\{{juiz_version}}` on Windows).
  On Windows, install it in PowerShell with
  `& ([scriptblock]::Create((irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenJUIZ/juiz/main/scripts/install-juiz-sdk.ps1))) {{juiz_version}}`

libjuiz_sdk must be the same version as juiz: juiz does not load a plugin that carries another version of libjuiz_sdk.
`CMakeLists.txt` asks for exactly `{{juiz_version}}`, and `app/juizapp.yaml` requires `juiz: "={{juiz_version}}"` for the same reason.
When you update juiz, install libjuiz_sdk of the new version and change both.
To use libjuiz_sdk in another directory, run `JUIZ_SDK_DIR=<dir> scripts/dev.sh` (or `cmake -D JUIZ_SDK_DIR=<dir>`).

