## Changing the .jidl

The build generates the C++ types of `{{idl_main}}` again when it changes (with `juiz idl`, so juiz must be in PATH when you build).
When you change the declarations, change the functions and the manifests in `src/{{name}}.cpp` and `app/app.conf` to match
(`juiz idl -g cpp-skeleton -o <dir> {{idl_main}}` writes the functions of all the declarations again, to copy from).
When the `.jidl` imports another file, add it to `DEPENDS` of `juiz_generate_types` in `CMakeLists.txt`.

## Versions

The package version is `0.1.0` in both `CMakeLists.txt` and `app/juizapp.yaml`. When you release a new version, change both.

## Plugins for several OSes in one package

Run `scripts/dev.sh --release` on each OS, collect the `app/plugins/<target>/` directories in one `app/plugins/`, and run `scripts/pack.sh --no-build`.
Each `app/plugins/<target>/` holds the plugin and libjuiz_sdk of that OS.
